{
    "background_story": "Amani was a young Maasai warrior from rural Kenya. In his community, 'oka' was a term of endearment and respect, reserved for those who demonstrated exceptional bravery and wisdom. Amani earned this title after single-handedly saving his village from a devastating drought. He spent countless hours trekking to distant lands, seeking knowledge and assistance from neighboring tribes. His perseverance paid off when he discovered a hidden underground water source, which he helped to develop into a sustainable irrigation system. Amani's selflessness and determination brought life back to the parched earth, earning him the admiration and gratitude of his people. From that day forward, he was known as Oka Amani, a hero and a symbol of hope for generations to come.",
